WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.135
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.135 --> 00:00:11.287
Hello and welcome to
Stanford Graduate School of Business,

00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:14.515
my name is Sawyer Clark and
I am a first year MBA here at the GSB.

00:00:14.515 --> 00:00:17.771
Some of my classmates and I are going to
show you around our campus today.

00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:22.579
[MUSIC]

00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:25.321
As we walk forward we're walking
away from the GSB residences,

00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:27.575
which are just across
the street in that direction.

00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:30.344
And we're heading into what's
called the Town Square,

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:33.584
this is very much the center of and
the lifeblood of our community.

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:38.501
You'll see people all around me, meeting
both students, faculty, classmates of

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:43.155
mine, as well as guests, or other people
that are affiliated with the school.

00:00:43.155 --> 00:00:47.882
To my left you’ll also see Cooper Cafe,
which is a coffee shop where many of my

00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:51.913
friends and myself meet to get
coffee between or before classes.

00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:56.500
Above Cooper Cafe are many of the faculty
offices, as well as the adverb wall

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.385
of change, which describes the many
ways we can change in life.

00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:04.033
To my right is Arbuckle Cafe,
which is the main dining hall for

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.726
all the students at the GSB.

00:01:05.726 --> 00:01:15.726
[MUSIC]

00:01:18.465 --> 00:01:20.866
&gt;&gt; My name is Carla Larin, I'm an MBA 1.

00:01:20.866 --> 00:01:25.559
Students use the Bass Library mostly for
studying and also for group projects.

00:01:25.559 --> 00:01:30.652
I like to go to the Bass Library to get
my case readings done before classes.

00:01:30.652 --> 00:01:31.842
And I also go weekly for

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.985
leadership coaching from my
Arbuckle leadership fellow.

00:01:34.985 --> 00:01:38.190
&gt;&gt; My name is Piyush Pratik, I'm an MBA 2.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:41.424
Classes at the GSB are taught
by both practitioners and

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:45.581
tenured faculty to provide both
research and industry perspective.

00:01:45.581 --> 00:01:50.278
What's great about the GSB is that we
don't have any one method of teaching,

00:01:50.278 --> 00:01:51.371
we have several.

00:01:51.371 --> 00:01:54.670
There are, of course,
the case methods and the lectures.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:58.924
But we also have a ton of experiencial
learning opportunities where we apply

00:01:58.924 --> 00:02:01.725
concepts learned in class
into actual projects.

00:02:01.725 --> 00:02:04.102
We don't just learn in
a traditional classroom,

00:02:04.102 --> 00:02:06.603
there are a lot of hands
on learning opportunities.

00:02:06.603 --> 00:02:11.263
Many of these courses take place at
the CoLab, where in fact I'm headed next.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:15.814
&gt;&gt; Hi, my name is Tamar Nisbett and
I'm an MBA 1 here at Stanford GSB.

00:02:15.814 --> 00:02:18.937
The CoLab is a community space
where Stanford GSB students and

00:02:18.937 --> 00:02:22.129
their cofounders can come together
to work on their startups.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:25.833
It's also an innovation hub where any
Standford student can get exposure

00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:26.917
to design thinking.

00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:30.040
The CoLab is home to classic
Stanford startup classes,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.372
like Startup Garage and Venture Studio.

00:02:32.372 --> 00:02:35.761
And huge companies,
like DoorDash, have come from it.

00:02:35.761 --> 00:02:39.257
One of my favorite companies that's being
worked on right now is called Praxis Lab.

00:02:39.257 --> 00:02:42.581
It's a diversity and
inclusion startup that uses AR and

00:02:42.581 --> 00:02:44.924
VR to help engender empathy in others.

00:02:44.924 --> 00:02:49.383
One of the best parts about the CoLab is
that it's open 24, 7 so when the coffee

00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:53.470
shop is closed everyone can come and
work on their start up together here.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:59.274
&gt;&gt; [INAUDIBLE] a second year
MBA student from India.

00:02:59.274 --> 00:03:03.565
We are here at the Arbuckle Dining
at the center of the GSB.

00:03:03.565 --> 00:03:08.828
With its indoor and outdoor seating this
part serves as a natural meeting point for

00:03:08.828 --> 00:03:13.782
me and my friends as we catch up over
lunch or dinner, discussing our future,

00:03:13.782 --> 00:03:18.071
working on our class projects,
and thinking about our failures.

00:03:18.071 --> 00:03:22.321
One of my favourite memories here
is catching up with my classmates,

00:03:22.321 --> 00:03:27.173
learning about their cultures, and
cuisines while we share lunch or dinner.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:32.488
Arbuckle has a variety of options to
choose from, ranging from grilled items,

00:03:32.488 --> 00:03:38.302
pizzas, salads, daily changing global
cuisine, seasonal soups, and fresh fish.

00:03:38.302 --> 00:03:41.062
I love that Arbuckle
also serves Indian food,

00:03:41.062 --> 00:03:44.332
something that I thought I
would miss when I move here.

00:03:44.332 --> 00:03:49.268
Right outside Arbuckle is the Monument
to Change art installation,

00:03:49.268 --> 00:03:52.851
it reminds me that the future
is always changing.

00:03:52.851 --> 00:03:56.221
And I've got to be
evolving to change lives,

00:03:56.221 --> 00:03:59.778
change organizations,
and change the world.

00:03:59.778 --> 00:04:02.918
&gt;&gt; Hi, I'm Renata Giarola, and
I'm an MBA 1 here at the GSB,

00:04:02.918 --> 00:04:06.256
I'm originally from Brazil, and
I moved here from Australia.

00:04:06.256 --> 00:04:11.602
Stanford students are known for whenever
we have the chance we go outside and

00:04:11.602 --> 00:04:15.373
study for meetings, for
preparing presentations.

00:04:15.373 --> 00:04:19.301
We always reading and doing, maximizing
our time outside, which is really great.

00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:22.223
I didn't realize that
the GSB campus would be so

00:04:22.223 --> 00:04:25.154
integrated with where
most of the people live.

00:04:25.154 --> 00:04:30.753
So it's awesome that we can go to class,
go to meetings, go to speaker events,

00:04:30.753 --> 00:04:35.698
host small group dinners,
everything within the same small radius.

00:04:35.698 --> 00:04:37.863
So there is no typical
day here at the GSB.

00:04:37.863 --> 00:04:42.197
What I love the most about living here at
Jack McDonough Hall is that not only it's

00:04:42.197 --> 00:04:45.446
super close to the GSB campus,
but it creates this amazing,

00:04:45.446 --> 00:04:47.185
beautiful sense of community.

00:04:47.185 --> 00:04:51.937
After a typical day here at the GSB I like
getting to my room and taking the time to

00:04:51.937 --> 00:04:56.634
really shut down and I usually do that
by journaling and writing about my day.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:59.212
[MUSIC]

00:04:59.212 --> 00:05:04.134
&gt;&gt; My name is Abioduri Buari, the great
thing about being a GSB student is

00:05:04.134 --> 00:05:08.738
being able to take classes at any
school at Stanford University.

00:05:08.738 --> 00:05:12.223
It gives you the opportunity to
explore the Stanford campus.

00:05:12.223 --> 00:05:15.608
[MUSIC]

00:05:15.608 --> 00:05:19.113
&gt;&gt; At Stanford Gradate School of
Business you are more than a student,

00:05:19.113 --> 00:05:21.398
you’re part of the vibrant GSB community.

00:05:21.398 --> 00:05:24.575
From your classroom experience
to your active social life,

00:05:24.575 --> 00:05:28.875
from forging great relationships with
classmates and faculty to becoming part of

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:32.443
the larger Stanford network you’ll
find endless possibilities.

00:05:32.443 --> 00:05:33.970
We hope to see you here.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.733
[MUSIC]

